# S-20 — Digital downloads (#32, #46, #94). Result 30 Sep 2026 (local, Development): all as expected.
# setup: the P0-4 301-page book uploaded as a private book_file and set on formative-guide's digital format
# purchase T3-26-001013 → dev trigger → paid → fulfilled; DigitalBookEffect: grant 5 downloads, line available; invoice issued
# #32 link → {url: {api}/v1/downloads/{token}, expiresAt: +10 min, remaining: 5} (token = grant ‖ customer ‖ expiry + HMAC)
# #46 download → 200 application/pdf, attachment formative-guide.pdf, no-store; 886 KB; 301/301 pages stamped
#   "نسخة خاصة بـ {buyer} — 05•••••001 — T3-26-001013 — لا يجوز نشرها"; first download 0.75 s (stamp + cache), then 0.02 s
#   (cached per grant in private downloads/{grant}.pdf); download_log rows with ip_hash
# downloads 2–5 → 200, 6th → 403 download.limit_reached; new link at the limit → 403
# #94 reset (admin, staff:resend) → downloadCount 0, audited; download works again
# another customer asking a link for the grant → 404; revoked grant → 410 download.revoked (download and reset);
# tampered payload / garbage token → 410 download.link_expired; the download rate policy answers 429 when hammered
@base = http://localhost:5080/v1
@token = <customer access token>
@admin = <admin access token>

### #32 Download link
POST {{base}}/me/downloads/{{grantId}}/link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### #46 Download (the link is the credential)
GET {{base}}/downloads/{{downloadToken}}

### #94 Reset (staff)
POST {{base}}/admin/download-grants/{{grantId}}/reset
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason":"customer changed device"}
